How about this?

44
00:04:06,220 --> 00:04:07,977
It's the best sword I ever forged.

45
00:04:08,060 --> 00:04:09,531
I call it my masterpiece.

46
00:04:11,020 --> 00:04:13,020
I don't know, it's a little light.

47
00:04:13,300 --> 00:04:14,200
It should be.

48
00:04:14,380 --> 00:04:16,615
I used a speed-type metal to forge it.

49
00:04:17,020 --> 00:04:19,860
I'd like to test it if
it's cool. Test it how?

50
00:04:20,300 --> 00:04:21,829
You know, it's durability.

51
00:04:23,720 --> 00:04:25,217
What the heck are you doing?

52
00:04:25,300 --> 00:04:27,417
If you break your sword,
I'm not responsible.

53
00:04:27,500 --> 00:04:29,500
If it breaks, then that's too bad!

54
00:04:43,320 --> 00:04:45,420
You broke my... masterpiece.

55
00:04:55,440 --> 00:04:57,060
The hell were you thinking?

56
00:04:57,600 --> 00:04:58,430
I'm sorry.

57
00:04:58,740 --> 00:05:00,937
I didn't think yours
was gonna break so easy.

58
00:05:01,020 --> 00:05:01,850
Honest.

59
00:05:01,933 --> 00:05:06,428
Are you saying my sword, my masterpiece
of a sword was labor than you thought?

60
00:05:06,740 --> 00:05:07,570
Yeah...

61
00:05:07,653 --> 00:05:08,483
something like that.

62
00:05:10,380 --> 00:05:11,615
For your information,

63
00:05:11,920 --> 00:05:13,517
if I had the right materials,

64
00:05:13,600 --> 00:05:15,097
I could make a buttload
of swords that would

65
