155
00:10:45,780 --> 00:10:46,680
You're insane.

156
00:10:47,600 --> 00:10:50,424
Maybe, but that's all I
got for ideas right now.

157
00:10:54,880 --> 00:10:55,710
No way.

158
00:11:07,240 --> 00:11:10,797
If I had more of a running start,
I probably would have made it.

159
00:11:10,880 --> 00:11:12,280
Yeah, I don't think so.

160
00:11:18,080 --> 00:11:19,962
This is kind of weird, isn't it?

161
00:11:20,520 --> 00:11:22,497
This wouldn't happen in real life.

162
00:11:22,580 --> 00:11:24,357
You know, going to strange places,

163
00:11:24,440 --> 00:11:27,793
meeting a total stranger, and
then sleeping next to them.

164
00:11:28,140 --> 00:11:30,877
I mean, you actually tried
running up that wall.

165
00:11:30,960 --> 00:11:33,254
You really are a weirdo, you know that?

166
00:11:33,460 --> 00:11:34,780
Well, excuse me.

167
00:11:41,060 --> 00:11:44,840
Kirito, can I ask you something?
Ask away. I'm all ears.

168
00:11:45,900 --> 00:11:48,724
Why did you risk your
life like that to save me?

169
00:11:50,040 --> 00:11:52,628
I can't just sit back
and watch someone die.

170
00:11:53,240 --> 00:11:55,887
I'd rather die alongside
him than do nothing.

171
00:11:56,460 --> 00:11:59,519
Especially if that's someone's
a girl like you, Liz.

172
00:12:00,560 --> 00:12:02,117
Wow, you really are an idiot!

173
00:12:02,200 --> 00:12:04,847
You're the only person
who'd think like that.

174
00:12:10,420 --> 00:12:12,000
Hey, hold my hand.

175
00:12:19,240 --> 00:12:20,070
Kay.

176
00:12:28,800 --> 00:12:29,960
It's so warm.

177
00:12:30,480 --> 00:12:31,310
Huh?

178
00:12:32,600 --> 00:12:36,835
Even though you and me are just these
ones and zeros in a virtual world.

179
00:12:37,460 --> 00:12:38,290
I know.

180
00:12:55,200 --> 00:12:56,030
What the?

181
00:13:04,940 --> 00:13:05,822
What you doing?

182
00:13:06,920 --> 00:13:07,960
Hmm? Here, look.

183
00:13:11,620 --> 00:13:13,920
Is this what I think it is?

184
00:13:14,720 --> 00:13:15,550
Uh-huh.

185
00:13:15,633 --> 00:13:17,397
It's that special metal
we came all this way for.

186
00:13:17,480 --> 00:13:22,068
Like you said, the dragon eats crystals,
and they turn to this in its stomach.

187
00:13:23,420 --> 00:13:25,067
No wonder it's hard to find.

188
00:13:25,200 --> 00:13:26,553
Yeah, but you found it.

189
00:13:27,200 --> 00:13:29,077
What's it doing down here, though?

190
00:13:29,160 --> 00:13:31,397
This hole isn't a trap like we thought.

191
00:13:31,480 --> 00:13:34,780
It's the dragon's nest. R-really? Uh-huh.

192
00:13:35,140 --> 00:13:38,197
And that's not just an ingot,
that's dragon excrement.

193
00:13:38,280 --> 00:13:39,820
You know, poop. Huh?

194
00:13:41,620 --> 00:13:42,450
Oh.

195
00:13:43,340 --> 00:13:44,170
Ah!

196
00:13:44,360 --> 00:13:47,397
Well, I guess this means we
got what we came here for.

197
00:13:47,480 --> 00:13:48,740
Still stuck, though.

198
00:13:51,080 --> 00:13:54,720
Wait, this is supposed to be
a dragon's nest, right? Yep.

199
00:13:55,060 --> 00:13:59,020
Because dragons are nocturnal, so
it won't be long before it comes.

200
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:04,830
It's here!

201
00:14:09,040 --> 00:14:09,897
What? What?

202
00:14:09,980 --> 00:14:10,957
