203
00:14:11,040 --> 00:14:11,870
No!

204
00:14:21,260 --> 00:14:22,800
Hang on to me, Liz!

205
00:14:32,320 --> 00:14:33,480
Almost there.

206
00:14:47,660 --> 00:14:48,490
Wow!

207
00:14:48,573 --> 00:14:49,440
Look at that!

208
00:15:00,920 --> 00:15:01,750
Kirito!

209
00:15:01,833 --> 00:15:02,900
You know what?

210
00:15:03,440 --> 00:15:04,380
Know what?

211
00:15:05,260 --> 00:15:06,560
Don't freak out!

212
00:15:06,760 --> 00:15:08,780
But I'm falling in love with you!

213
00:15:10,480 --> 00:15:11,715
I can't hear a thing!

214
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:13,300
What did you just say?

215
00:15:14,760 --> 00:15:16,220
Never mind!

216
00:15:27,300 --> 00:15:30,000
A one-handed longsword, right? Yup.

217
00:15:30,500 --> 00:15:31,441
Make it awesome.

218
00:15:43,940 --> 00:15:45,460
I didn't imagine it.

219
00:15:45,860 --> 00:15:47,820
The warmth of Kirito's hands.

220
00:15:48,240 --> 00:15:49,460
The way I feel.

221
00:15:50,680 --> 00:15:53,151
As soon as I've made the best sword I can,

222
00:15:54,040 --> 00:15:54,870
I'll tell him.

223
00:15:58,660 --> 00:15:59,490
Whoa.

224
00:16:13,700 --> 00:16:15,940
The sword is called Dark Repulsor.

225
00:16:16,340 --> 00:16:17,460
One of a kind.

226
00:16:17,840 --> 00:16:20,664
And it's not even in the
Infobroker's directory.

227
00:16:21,460 --> 00:16:23,420
Go on, try it. Okay.

228
00:16:30,480 --> 00:16:31,680
Good? Bad?

229
00:16:32,020 --> 00:16:33,180
It's real heavy.

230
00:16:33,420 --> 00:16:35,540
It's a good sword. Yay!

231
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:38,529
It feels like you forged
your soul into it.

232
00:16:46,160 --> 00:16:48,197
Okay, you held up your end of the deal.

233
00:16:48,280 --> 00:16:51,077
It's time for me to pay up, so how much?

234
00:16:51,160 --> 00:16:56,437
Um, well, I don't really need any money.

235
00:16:56,520 --> 00:16:59,817
Instead,

236
00:16:59,900 --> 00:17:03,997
I'd like to be your exclusive
blacksmith from now on.

237
00:17:04,080 --> 00:17:07,080
What do you mean? Exclusive?

238
00:17:10,260 --> 00:17:11,090
What's wrong?

239
00:17:12,620 --> 00:17:13,450
I mean.

240
00:17:14,040 --> 00:17:17,897
Anytime you get back from the field, stop
by and let me do maintenance on your gear.

241
00:17:17,980 --> 00:17:18,810
Every day.

242
00:17:18,893 --> 00:17:20,260
From now till the end.

243
00:17:24,080 --> 00:17:24,920
Liz I

244
00:17:25,680 --> 00:17:26,510
Kirito

245
00:17:26,900 --> 00:17:27,730
I just

246
00:17:28,680 --> 00:17:29,510
I

247
00:17:30,520 --> 00:17:32,760
Liz I was so worried

248
00:17:33,820 --> 00:17:36,880
Asuna Liz Where were you last night?

249
00:17:36,980 --> 00:17:41,197
I tried messaging you, but you didn't
answer and I couldn't track you on the map!

250
00:17:41,280 --> 00:17:44,840
Sorry, I kinda got stuck
in a dungeon. A dungeon?

251
00:17:45,120 --> 00:17:46,591
You went all by yourself?

252
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:47,830
Uh-uh.

253
00:17:47,913 --> 00:17:48,743
I went with him.

254
00:17:50,700 --> 00:17:51,530
Kirito?

255
00:17:53,520 --> 00:17:54,350
Hey, Asuna.

256
00:17:54,433 --> 00:17:55,460
Long time no see.

257
00:17:55,700 --> 00:17:57,700
It's been what, like two days?

258
00:17:58,000 --> 00:17:59,417
Well, this is a surprise.

259
00:17:59,500 --> 00:18:01,477
I didn't know you wanted
to check this place out.

260
00:18:01,560 --> 00:18:04,237
I wish you would have told me
I could have come with you.

261
00:18:04,320 --> 00:18:05,555
I'm sort of confused.

262
00:18:05,640 --> 00:18:06,717
Do you know each other?

263
00:18:06,800 --> 00:18:09,780
Yeah, both of us are on
the assault team, so...

264
00:18:11,040 --> 00:18:13,717
He said he was looking to
get a more powerful sword.

265
00:18:13,800 --> 00:18:16,380
So I told him about you and your shop. Oh.

266
00:18:16,900 --> 00:18:18,417
Why is she acting like that?

267
00:18:18,500 --> 00:18:20,297
I swear, if you did
anything weird to her...

268
00:18:20,380 --> 00:18:21,760
I didn't do anything.

269
00:18:21,960 --> 00:18:24,136
Then why'd you stutter just now, huh?

270
00:18:24,380 --> 00:18:27,137
You know, you could try to
show a little more compassion.

271
00:18:27,220 --> 00:18:28,396
I almost got killed.

272
00:18:28,600 --> 00:18:29,860
Like that's my fault!

273
00:18:30,120 --> 00:18:32,591
Don't I always tell you not to fight Solo?

274
00:18:32,920 --> 00:18:33,750
Right.

275
00:18:34,400 --> 00:18:35,440
I get it now.

276
00:18:37,040 --> 00:18:40,158
If this guy said anything
rude, you'd tell me, right?

277
00:18:42,060 --> 00:18:42,890
Liz?

278
00:18:46,160 --> 00:18:47,837
Do you want to talk about rude?

279
00:18:47,920 --> 00:18:48,750
Try this.

280
00:18:48,833 --> 00:18:52,017
First thing he does when he comes
in is shatter my best sword.

281
00:18:52,100 --> 00:18:53,280
What? I'm sorry.

282
00:18:53,800 --> 00:18:54,630
Oh, come on.

283
00:18:54,720 --> 00:18:57,132
You don't have to apologize for anything.

284
00:18:57,520 --> 00:19:00,814
He might be a little weird,
but he's not such a bad guy.

285
00:19:00,980 --> 00:19:02,517
Don't screw this up, Asuna.

286
00:19:02,600 --> 00:19:03,430
He's a keeper.

287
00:19:04,420 --> 00:19:06,480
But I told you, it's not like that!

288
00:19:07,760 --> 00:19:08,590
Liz?

289
00:19:08,673 --> 00:19:10,637
Sorry, I have to go pick up some supplies.

290
00:19:10,720 --> 00:19:11,817
I'll be right back.

291
00:19:11,900 --> 00:19:13,880
But you're gonna leave the store?

292
00:19:14,200 --> 00:19:17,260
Hold down the fort for me. Later! What?

293
00:19:17,520 --> 00:19:18,580
No, wait, Liz!

294
00:19:37,620 --> 00:19:38,450
Lisbeth.

295
00:19:45,100 --> 00:19:46,800
I almost got away with it.

296
00:19:49,840 --> 00:19:51,320
A couple more minutes,

297
00:19:51,960 --> 00:19:55,080
and I would have gone back
to my usual cheerful self.

298
00:19:55,500 --> 00:19:56,880
Liz, I...

299
00:19:57,900 --> 00:19:59,429
How'd you know I was here?

300
00:20:03,940 --> 00:20:06,705
I scanned the whole town
for you from up there.

301
00:20:08,040 --> 00:20:10,569
Figures you'd do
something crazy like that.

302
00:20:16,340 --> 00:20:17,840
Sorry if I worried you.

303
00:20:18,140 --> 00:20:19,140
I'm fine now.

304
00:20:19,660 --> 00:20:21,248
Must be all the excitement.

305
00:20:21,780 --> 00:20:23,780
I'm not used to having adventures.

306
00:20:25,840 --> 00:20:29,020
Anyway, I'll just forget
everything I said.

307
00:20:29,760 --> 00:20:30,590
Okay?

308
00:20:32,560 --> 00:20:33,657
Liz, I...

309
00:20:33,740 --> 00:20:35,840
I just wanted to thank you.

310
00:20:37,100 --> 00:20:38,217
See, I...

311
00:20:38,300 --> 00:20:39,660
I don't know.

312
00:20:40,280 --> 00:20:43,986
I always thought dying was better
than surviving day after day.

313
00:20:44,640 --> 00:20:45,934
Living with the guilt.

314
00:20:47,920 --> 00:20:48,750
Kirito.

315
00:20:49,120 --> 00:20:53,960
But then, we got stuck in that hole, and
I was really happy we were still alive.

316
00:20:54,420 --> 00:20:58,300
I realized that even here, our
lives are real and have meaning.

317
00:20:58,860 --> 00:21:00,997
Thank you for helping me see that, Liz.

318
00:21:01,080 --> 00:21:04,237
I guess it's what I've been
looking for this whole time.

319
00:21:04,320 --> 00:21:05,150
Yeah, me too.

320
00:21:05,960 --> 00:21:07,177
I know what you mean.

321
00:21:07,260 --> 00:21:09,077
I was also looking for something.

322
00:21:09,160 --> 00:21:10,042
Something real.

323
00:21:10,360 --> 00:21:11,540
Hoping I'd find it.

324
00:21:13,020 --> 00:21:14,540
The warmth of your hand.

325
00:21:15,140 --> 00:21:17,700
For me, that was real.

326
00:21:23,140 --> 00:21:24,500
Do me a favor, okay?

327
00:21:24,960 --> 00:21:26,901
Tell us to know what you told me.

328
00:21:27,100 --> 00:21:27,930
Liz.

329
00:21:28,980 --> 00:21:30,517
I'm fine, really.

330
00:21:30,600 --> 00:21:33,659
The getting over it part,
that's gonna take a while.

331
00:21:37,920 --> 00:21:39,657
Until I do, promise me.

332
00:21:39,740 --> 00:21:41,737
Promise me you'll put
an end to this world.

333
00:21:41,820 --> 00:21:45,200
Till then, I'll keep doing what I do best.

334
00:21:46,580 --> 00:21:48,100
I promise I will.

335
00:21:48,580 --> 00:21:50,180
I swear I'll beat the game.

336
00:21:54,360 --> 00:21:57,837
If you ever need your weapons or
gear repaired, my door's always open.

337
00:21:57,920 --> 00:21:58,750
Sure.

338
00:21:59,280 --> 00:22:00,360
Don't forget now.

339
00:22:00,520 --> 00:22:02,277
You'll always be welcome at my shop.

340
00:22:02,360 --> 00:22:03,460
Thank you.

341
00:22:43,280 --> 00:22:46,080
Thank you.

342
00:23:36,080 --> 00:23:38,786
Next time, the sword
dance of black and white.
